<title>UK: Freddie Mac prices $500 mln 10-year global bond.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac prices $500 mln 10-year global bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac) priced a $500 million 10-year global bond, joint lead managers Goldman Sachs and Nomura Securities said.</p>
<p>The bonds will pay a 6.70 percent coupon, and issue and reoffer prices is 99.875.</p>
<p>The spread is 21 basis points over the yield of the 10-year Treasury note.</p>
<p>The paper matures on January 5, 2007. The coupon payment dates are on January 5 and July 5. The payment date will be on January 14.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
